Kubernetes network policy

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:14.680
that prevents external traffic
from reaching the container.

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:18.210
This network policy is defined
in the Kubernetes configuration

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.910
file that is stored in
Hipster Shop's Anthos Config

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.720
Management repository.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.980
As Drishti explained
earlier, Hipster Shop

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:29.070
is using their own
instance of GitLab

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:32.250
running on GKE to host their
Anthos Config Management

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.850
repository.

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.510
This repository contains
Kubernetes configuration

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.730
and policy files that
are automatically

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:40.980
applied to Hipster Shop's
staging and production

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.060
clusters.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.980
And the configurations
and policies

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.370
are kept in sync with this
source of truth repository

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:51.040
to prevent any unwarranted
deletions or changes.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.085
The Anthos config
management repository

00:09:53.085 --> 00:09:54.900
is structured in
a way that allows

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.390
me to apply configuration
and policies

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:01.350
across all clusters at an
individual cluster level

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.110
or at a namespace level.

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:06.660
If I go to the directory for
the namespace that contains

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.210
the hipster legacy
CRM application,

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:13.830
I can open the
network-policy.yaml,

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.560
and I'll see the policy that
is currently preventing me from

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:21.590
